<name>SANO, SATOSHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAGUCHI, NOBUYASU</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IWAMOTO YASUHIDE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKAZAWA FUMIHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SANO SATOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMAGUCHI NOBUYASU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IWAMOTO, YASUHIDE</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAZAWA, FUMIHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SANO, SATOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAGUCHI, NOBUYASU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An optical scanning type touch panel comprises an optical unit, which is an integral structure comprising a light-emitting element that emits infrared laser light; a collimation lens that collimates the laser light from the light-emitting element; a photodetector element that receives scanning light; a slit board that limits the incident light to the photodetector element; a polygon mirror for angular scanning of the laser light from the light-emitting element; an aperture mirror that limits light projected from the collimation lens to the polygon mirror using an aperture and reflects the light reflected by the polygon mirror toward the photodetector element; a lens that converges the light reflected by the aperture mirror; and a motor that rotates the polygon mirror.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur un écran tactile à balayage optique comprenant une unité optique comportant: un laser émetteur d'IR; une lentille collimatant la lumière émise par le laser; un photodétecteur recevant la lumière balayée; une plaque fendue limitant la lumière incidente frappant le photodétecteur; un miroir polygonal effectuant un balayage angulaire de la lumière de l'émetteur laser; un miroir à ouverture limitant la lumière projetée par les lentilles collimatrices vers le miroir polygonal et réfléchissant la lumière réfléchie par le miroir polygonal vers l'élément photodétecteur; une lentille faisant converger la lumière réfléchie par le miroir à ouverture; et un moteur faisant tourner le miroir polygonal.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>